  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia: Somalia Criminal Investigation Programme (SOMCIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To provide investigators at Federal and Federal Member States levels with advanced knowledge required to conduct investigation in line with international standards and the Somali Provisional Constitution. 2) To provide justice actors in Mogadishu with a case management system and technical knowledge required to conduct their case recording, processing and information-sharing activities electronically.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Criminal investigators, Criminal Investigation Departments and Units of the Somali Police Force at Federal and Federal Member States (FMS) levels and all criminal justice institutions active in Mogadishu and the FMS. Indirect beneficiaries: Wider population of Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enable the Somali Police to provide improved safety and security to the local population.</narrative>
  </description>
